Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:11:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/52] fix(ui): no getting-started checklist in the reviewer
 UI, or before the canvas loads

The getting-started checklist (connect an agent, give it a task) showed for
a moment on opening a canvas and then went away. The role reads as edit
until the canvas has loaded (grantedRole falls back to edit), so the
editor mounted the checklist straight away and unmounted it once the real
role, or a phone's review cap, arrived.

Two changes. The reviewer UI (FULL_UI off) has nothing of the agents, so it
has no agent onboarding either. With FULL_UI on the checklist waits for the
canvas, and so for the real role, before it shows.

The reviewer layout test now also checks that no Getting started card is
there. It fails without this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/pages/CanvasPage.tsx            | 6 +++++-
 tests/reviewerLayoutBrowser.test.ts | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/pages/CanvasPage.tsx b/src/pages/CanvasPage.tsx
index 64e4637..f455070 100644
--- a/src/pages/CanvasPage.tsx
+++ b/src/pages/CanvasPage.tsx
@@ -1165,7 +1165,11 @@ export function CanvasPage({
           {/* the presence pill in the bar already carries each agent's status
               line; this per-agent stack is only for windows too narrow for it */}
           {!reviewerLayout && <WorkingNow style={{ left: chrome.left }} className="min-[1180px]:hidden" />}
-          {!readOnly && <Onboarding canvasId={canvasId} />}
+          {/* the getting-started checklist is about connecting an agent: not part
+              of the reviewer UI, and only once the canvas (and so the role) has
+              loaded, since the role reads as edit until then and the card would
+              show for a moment and vanish for a reviewer */}
+          {FULL_UI && canvas && !readOnly && <Onboarding canvasId={canvasId} />}
           <AccessBanner guest={guest} onSignUp={onSignUp} onSignIn={onSignIn} />
           {!isMobile &&
             (layersOpen ? (
